# record-declared-and-observed — the proposing actor's token declares risk
# `low`, but the gate's declared floor is `high` (SPEC §4: a gate's floor is
# the maximum of the computed risk and the floor, a raise-only step). The
# reservation guards on the raised, gate-computed risk, so the low-declared
# token is in fact reserved. SPEC §7.4 requires the log entry to carry both
# the declared token and the host-observed facts that produced the
# gate-computed risk, so that redress weighs what was claimed against what
# was observed rather than a reconciled value (PROM-001) — this vector pins
# that both appear in the log, not only the final verdict.
actor bot7
human legal role legal
gate  decide risk high grant bot7
reserve automated_decision by legal when risk >= high
cord  bot7   -> decide
cord  decide -> master
